# Line endings are LF everywhere, including on Windows checkouts.
#
# Not a style preference. `reference/baseline-*.txt` are compared against fresh
# tool output by `tools/gate.mjs`, and the tools emit LF on every platform — so
# a CRLF checkout would make every gate report a difference on every line. The
# gate strips \r defensively for exactly this reason, but the honest fix is for
# the file on disk to match the file the tool produces.
#
# The same argument covers the shaders: GLSL lives inside JS template literals,
# so a stray \r ends up in the source string handed to the driver.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Contact sheets and any other capture that gets committed are binary.
*.png binary
